e stone sighed open after a thousand years.\n\nInside: wonders. the engineer Marco, the scholar at heart, wept at the murals. Casey Drake kept watch, because wonders in such places usually have teeth. They did: the floor was a trap, the walls were a trap, the air was a trap."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Price of Gold', 'text': "the smuggler queen was delivered to the authorities with the evidence. a pharaoh's seal was delivered to the museum, on loan, with Casey Drake's name on the plaque and the engineer Marco's name right beside it, where it belonged.\n\nThe backup team wasn't loyal — just paid. When Casey Drake offered them the truth about the smuggler queen's promises (empty) versus a share of the legitimate expedition rights (real), they lowered their weapons. Money talks. Truth talks louder.\n\nthe smuggler queen, bound and furious, offered everything: money, power, a share. Casey Drake listened politely and said no politely, which infuriated the smuggler queen more than any insult. Some people can't be bought. Some treasures can't be sold."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Real Treasure', 'text': "the smuggler queen got fifteen years and a memoir deal. Casey Drake got the kid's wide eyes and the engineer Marco's friendship and a new map already arriving by courier. No return address. Of course.\n\nThe museum opening was black tie. Casey Drake wore boots. the engineer Marco, recovered and insufferable, wore a grin. a pharaoh's seal sat behind glass, humming faintly, home at last among people who'd care for it.\n\nThey stood before a pharaoh's seal one last time. It had started all this: the legend, the race, the ruin, the rescue. Casey Drake saluted it. Some doors, once opened, stay open forever."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'Next Horizon', 'text': "Somewhere, the smuggler queen was reading about it in a cell and planning. Let them. The world is wide, and Casey Drake is faster, and the engineer Marco is smarter, and that's usually enough.\n\nCasey Drake took one last look at the